1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,500
In modern automotive bays and high-voltage battery assembly lines,

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:10,200
technicians are surrounded by heavy machinery, grease, and high-voltage risks.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,800
Typing on diagnostic laptops with insulated gloves is cumbersome,

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,200
inefficient, and dangerous. Every second spent away from the vehicle

5
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:23,500
increases downtime and safety hazards.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Meet AutoCopilot: the first real-time, hands-free voice agent

7
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:33,000
purpose-built for automotive diagnostics and industrial operations.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,500
AutoCopilot connects live CAN-FD telemetry and ISO safety manuals

9
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:43,200
through an ultra-low-latency voice interface powered by AssemblyAI.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Traditional voice models fail in noisy garages and choke on acronyms

11
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,500
like UDS 0x19, CAN-FD, and ISO 26262.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,500
We leveraged AssemblyAI Universal-3 Pro with customized Word Boost,

13
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:00,800
achieving near 100% accuracy on complex diagnostic terms.

14
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:05,800
Our WebRTC pipeline streams 16kHz raw PCM audio over WebSockets

15
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,500
with 450ms VAD silence detection for crisp, human-like turn-taking.

16
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,000
Now let's see AutoCopilot in live diagnostic action.

17
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
"AutoCopilot, query active DTCs and check coolant temperature."

18
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,500
Watch the right-hand panel: in less than 50 milliseconds,

19
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:30,200
AutoCopilot executes parallel tool calls across the physical CAN bus

20
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,000
and our vector database for workshop manuals.

21
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:39,000
"Diagnostic trouble code P0117 detected. Coolant temperature

22
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:43,800
is 104.2°C, approaching critical thermal threshold."

23
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:49,500
The live telemetry gauges instantly respond, updating temperature,

24
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:53,000
bus voltage, and DTC logs in real time.

25
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Now for our biggest highlight: zero-latency Barge-in.

26
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:03,000
In noisy, fast-paced shops, waiting for an AI to finish speaking is unacceptable.

27
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:07,800
As the CoPilot begins reading: "According to ISO 26262 ASIL-B..."

28
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:12,000
I interrupt: "Wait, stop! What is the emergency shutoff procedure?"

29
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:16,800
Boom! Notice the red INTERRUPTED badge: within 18 milliseconds,

30
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,200
AssemblyAI PartialTranscript triggered our speech cancellation,

31
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:25,500
cutting TTS playback instantly without jarring speech overlap.

32
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
AutoCopilot transforms industrial maintenance from tedious manual typing

33
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,800
into a natural, high-speed conversational dialogue.

34
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:38,200
Zero-latency voice, domain-specific accuracy, and parallel execution.

35
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:43,000
AutoCopilot: keeping hands on tools, eyes on machines,

36
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:47,500
and industrial engineering safer and faster than ever. Thank you!
